      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Hard to knock winning form with THE CABLE GUY (1) who has looked good winning his past two, backing up the maiden win with a tough effort over this track and trip. Up in grade again but it looks another lovely option and he can prove too good again. LIMBERING (9) is a 9yo veteran mare who didn't fire last time at Gawler but had been good prior and could surprise with no weight from a good draw. DRUNKEN SAILOR (7) is another that can mix form, the second two back here behind THE CABLE GUY has him right in the mix. OSTRICA (3) won her maiden nicely here fresh, struggling at Bendigo last time. She can bounce back here. BLUE TYPHOON (6) was okay fresh in a tougher race and can improve.",
